    "Stem": "Northfield Industries implemented a new entity-wide internal control framework 18 months ago. The internal audit function recently surveyed 200 employees across all departments and levels. Survey results: 78% of respondents could not identify a single internal control for which they are personally responsible, 62% reported they have never received any training on internal controls, and 45% said they do not know whom to contact if they observe a control weakness or suspected misconduct. Separately, management confirms that an updated 45-page Control Procedures Manual was distributed to all 32 department heads via email 16 months ago, with a cover memo instructing them to share relevant sections with their teams. No training sessions were conducted, no acknowledgment of receipt was required, and no follow-up assessment was performed to determine whether employees understood their control responsibilities. Analyze this situation: which element of COSO Principle 14 is most clearly violated, and what communication strategy would most effectively address the gap?",
